{
  "name": "Ball Pit",
  "notes": "Objects a room can knock about. Eight balls of varying size sit at the bottom of a dim tube; a bass hit kicks the lot of them, they collide on the way up and on the way down, and they settle again on their own -- nothing has to keep telling them to. The band drives `kick` as well as firing it, so a soft hit lifts them a little and a loud one throws them at the far end. Mass is the radius, so the big ones plough through the small ones rather than trading places with them. The `L1` block underneath is not decoration: without a lit tube the balls read as sparks in the dark instead of as things in a container.",
